---
import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { contactEmail } from "../config";

const email = contactEmail();
---
<Prose title="Privacy" changed="20 October 2026">
  <p class="mt-4">
    This page explains what Road to Sixty keeps about you, where it's stored, who can see it, and how to have it removed. We keep only what syncing
    your journeys needs. Nothing is public, and nothing is sold.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The addon on its own</h2>
    <p>The addon saves everything in your own World of Warcraft folder. Nothing leaves your computer unless you install the app and link it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the app sends</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your BattleTag, to show which account a PC is linked to.</li>
      <li>Your Battle.net account number, scrambled with a secret key before it's stored, so the number itself is never kept.</li>
      <li>Each character's name, realm and journey: where it went, quests, kills, levels and gear.</li>
      <li>
        The players each character grouped with: their name, race, class, level and guild, where and when you first met, and the time and dungeons
        you shared.
      </li>
      <li>For each linked PC: the name you gave it, whether it's a Mac, Windows or Linux, and its app and addon versions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
    <p>
      Your account and journeys are kept on our servers, and everything travels over encrypted connections. We keep your data until you delete it.
      For each character we keep the last 100 versions of its journey, and one a week from before that. Backups are deleted after 30 days.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
      Only you, through the app on a PC you've linked. Nothing is shown publicly, and we never sell or share your data. We access stored data only
      when running or repairing the service needs it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deleting it</h2>
    <p>
      In the app, open Account and choose Delete everything. Your account and every journey are removed from our servers at once, and from backups
      within 30 days. Journeys on your own PCs stay. You can download each character's latest journey first, from the same screen.
    </p>
    <p>
      To remove just one character, open it in the app's Characters list and choose Remove from backup. An earlier journey of a character, from
      before an Erase or from a deleted character with the same name, is removed the same way. Beta characters are listed separately, with one
      button to remove them all.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies. The sign-in page sets one when you link a PC. Only that page uses it, and it expires within a week.</p>
    <p>
      We count visits with Vercel Web Analytics: which pages were viewed, and the country, browser and kind of device. It sets no cookies, and it
      can't tell who you are or follow you to other sites.
    </p>
    <p>
      Vercel hosts this site and Cloudflare serves the downloads. Like any web host, they see your IP address and browser when you visit, and keep
      their own logs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Battle.net</h2>
    <p>
      Signing in goes through Blizzard's Battle.net. We receive only your account number and BattleTag, never your password. Road to Sixty isn't
      affiliated with Blizzard Entertainment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For a copy of your data, a correction, deletion, or any question about this page, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. If this page
      changes, the date at the top changes with it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Prose>
